==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|prō-|dūcō|gloss2=lead; draw}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|prōdūcō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|prōdūcō|prōdūcere|prōdūxī|prōductum|conj=3|pattern=short-imp}}

# I [[lead]] or [[bring]] forth, forward or out.
# I [[conduct]] to; bring before, [[present]].
# I draw or [[stretch]] out, [[lengthen]], [[extend]].
# I [[bring to light]], [[disclose]], [[expose]].
# I [[advance]], [[draw out]].
# I bring forth, [[bear]], [[beget]]; [[bring up]], [[rear]], [[educate]].
# I [[expose]] for [[sale]].
# I [[place]] one thing before another.
# {{lb|la|grammar|of pronunciation}} I lengthen, [[prolong]].
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} I bring into [[use]], make, [[invent]] [[devise]], [[produce]].
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} I [[raise]], [[promote]], [[advance]].
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} I lead or [[induce]] someone to do something, [[entice]].
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} I draw or [[drag out]], lengthen out, prolong, [[protract]].
# {{lb|la|figuratively|of time}} I [[pass]], [[spend]].
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} I [[plant]], [[cultivate]].

